Q: How to load local HTML files in Xamarin Forms WebView A: <p>Here is related post and official sample</p>

<p>See if this can help.</p>

<p><a href="https://stackoverflow.com/questions/38055244/how-to-load-a-local-html-file-in-a-xamrian-forms-webview/43268968#43268968">Xamarin load local html</a></p>

<p>and</p>

<p><a href="https://github.com/xamarin/xamarin-forms-samples/tree/master/WorkingWithWebview" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Official sample here</a> </p>

<pre><code>public LocalHtmlBaseUrl ()
    {
        var browser = new BaseUrlWebView (); // temporarily use this so we can custom-render in iOS

        var htmlSource = new HtmlWebViewSource ();

        htmlSource.Html = @"&lt;html&gt;...&lt;/html&gt;";

        htmlSource.BaseUrl = DependencyService.Get&lt;IBaseUrl&gt; ().Get ();


        browser.Source = htmlSource;

        Content = browser;
    }
</code></pre>

Q: how to remove hover on click A: <p>You should simplify the bindings to just target them a little more generically, then remove the hover classes on all of them:</p>

<pre><code>$(".respuesta").on("click", function (index) {
  $(this).removeClass("hover");
  // do other things
});
</code></pre>

<p>You can also use the index to find which number they are if they're in a list. </p>

<p>if you want the hover to not override the click, give the click an active class and tell the hovers to work on everything but them:</p>

<pre><code>$('.respuesta:not(.active)').hover(function() {
  // do something
}
</code></pre>

