Q: Incoming BLE L2CAP SDU not reported to Delegate A: <p>command line apps require the run loop to be started explicitly: <code>CFRunLoopRun();</code>  however the runloop will only run for as long as at least one runloop source or timer is associated with it.  the l2cap streams become runloop sources asynchronously by which time the runloop may have died.  so, before starting the runloop try something like:</p>
<pre><code>CFRunLoopRef mainrunloop = CFRunLoopGetCurrent();
CFFileDescriptorContext context = {1, &amp;mainrunloop, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL };
int fd = fcntl(STDIN_FILENO,F_DUPFD, 0);
CFFileDescriptorRef kybfd = CFFileDescriptorCreate(kCFAllocatorDefault, fd, false, call_bak, context);
CFFileDescriptorEnableCallBacks(kybfd, kCFFileDescriptorReadCallBack);
CFRunLoopSourceRef kybsource = CFFileDescriptorCreateRunLoopSource(kCFAllocatorDefault, kybdfd, 0);
CFRunLoopAddSource(mainrunloop, kybsource, kCFRunLoopDefaultMode);
</code></pre>
<p>where <code>call_bak</code> is a routine that reads from stdin.</p>
